>> title: Kinpira Gobō
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: japanese, burdock, carrot, sesame, make ahead, side, vegetarian
>> counters: Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: きんぴらごぼう, kinpira gobō, kinpira gobo, キンピラごぼう, 金平牛蒡, burdock and carrot, braised burdock, sesame burdock
>> pairs-with: gohan, saba-shioyaki
>> servings: 4
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: forgiving — about three days in the fridge and a month in the freezer, and it is better on the second day; what shortens it is stopping while there is still liquid in the pan, because wet kinpira sours by day two
>> step.1: Four ingredients and three operations, and that is the correct size for it. The knife work is the recipe: matchsticks of the same thickness cook at the same speed, and a shaved gobo tastes different from a chopped one.
>> step.2: soak 5 min, drain
>> step.3: fry hard 3 min
>> step.4: cook dry 4 min
>> step.5: toss through off the heat

Four ingredients and three operations, and that is the correct size for it — not a simplified version of something bigger. The knife work is what makes it: matchsticks of one thickness cook at one speed, and a gobo shaved at an angle tastes different from a gobo chopped square.

Soak @burdock root{7%oz}(200 g; scraped with the back of a knife, never peeled, cut into matchsticks) in @cold water{4%cups}(950 mL; changed once) ~soak{5%min}, until the water browns. That colour is the tannin that would otherwise turn the whole dish grey.

Fry @&(~1)drained gobo{} with @carrot{1}(cut into matchsticks the same size) and @dried red chile{1}(seeded, in rings) in @toasted sesame oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) in a #frying pan{} over a high flame ~fry{3%min}, until the gobo turns from white to faintly translucent.

Pour @soy sauce{1 1/2%Tbs}(22 mL), @mirin{1 1/2%Tbs}(22 mL), @sake{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and @sugar{2%tsp} over @&(~1)vegetables{} and ~cook{4%min}, tossing, until the pan is dry and every stick is lacquered. Dry is not a preference here; it is what makes it keep.

Toss @toasted sesame seeds{1%Tbs}(crushed between your palms as they go in) through @&(~1)kinpira{} off the heat.
